#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:163
msgid "—"
msgstr "—"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:165
msgid ""
"2つの式の :math:`a_0` の差は0.0001 Åで、Birch–Murnaghanの式では当てはめる範囲を13点から7点に狭めても "
":math:`a_0` は変わりません。\\ Birch–Murnaghanの式のほうが残差が1桁小さく、13点のエネルギーを0.005 "
"meV以内で再現します。\\ 2次式と違い、Birch–Murnaghanの式は範囲を広げても値がずれないので、極小から離れた点も含めて安定に "
":math:`a_0` を決められます。\\ 以下では、Birch–Murnaghanの式の値 :math:`a_0=3.6303` "
"Åを、エネルギー曲線から求めた格子定数とします。"
msgstr ""
"The values of :math:`a_0` from the two equations differ by 0.0001 Å, and "
"for the Birch–Murnaghan equation, narrowing the fitting range from 13 to "
"7 points leaves :math:`a_0` unchanged. \\ The Birch–Murnaghan equation "
"gives residuals an order of magnitude smaller and reproduces the energies"
" of all 13 points to within 0.005 meV. \\ Unlike the quadratic fit, the "
"Birch–Murnaghan equation gives a value that does not shift as the fitting"
" range widens, so it determines :math:`a_0` stably even when points far "
"from the minimum are included. \\ Below, we use the Birch–Murnaghan "
"result :math:`a_0=3.6303` Å as the lattice constant obtained from the "
"energy curve."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:173
msgid "SCFの圧力とPulay応力"
msgstr "SCF Pressure and Pulay Stress"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:175
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"応力から格子定数を求める ``vc-relax`` （ :numref:`{number}節 <sec-cl-vcrelax>` "
"）は、SCF計算の圧力が0になる格子を探します。\\ そこでまず、SCF計算の圧力がエネルギー曲線の傾きと一致するかを、 :numref"
":`fig-cl-eos` の右の図で比べます。\\ SCF計算の出力の圧力 :math:`P` （ ``P=`` "
"）は、波動関数から直接計算した応力で、エネルギーの体積微分 :math:`P=-\\mathrm{d}E/\\mathrm{d}V` "
"にあたります。\\ 右の図で、SCFの圧力（青い点）と、当てはめた曲線を微分した圧力（灰色の曲線）はよく重なっています。\\ "
"SCFの圧力から当てはめた曲線の圧力を引くと、13点すべてで −0.67〜−0.33 kbar、極小付近では −0.44 "
"kbarで、SCFの圧力がわずかに小さくなっています。\\ SCFの圧力が0になる格子定数は3.6298 Åで、エネルギー曲線の極小（3.6303"
" Å）より0.0005 Å小さくなります。\\ 極小付近では、圧力は格子定数1 Åあたり約1100 kbar変わるので、0.44 "
"kbarの差が格子定数の0.0004 Åに相当します。"
msgstr ""
"``vc-relax`` (:numref:`Section {number} <sec-cl-vcrelax>`), which "
"determines the lattice constant from stress, searches for the lattice at "
"which the SCF pressure is zero. \\ We therefore first check, using the "
"right panel of :numref:`fig-cl-eos`, whether the SCF pressure agrees with"
" the slope of the energy curve. \\ The pressure :math:`P` (``P=``) in the"
" SCF output is the stress calculated directly from the wave functions and"
" corresponds to the volume derivative of the energy, "
":math:`P=-\\mathrm{d}E/\\mathrm{d}V`. \\ In the right panel, the SCF "
"pressures (blue points) closely overlap with the pressure obtained by "
"differentiating the fitted curve (gray curve). \\ Subtracting the "
"pressure of the fitted curve from the SCF pressure gives −0.67 to −0.33 "
"kbar across all 13 points and −0.44 kbar near the minimum; the SCF "
"pressure is slightly lower. \\ The SCF pressure reaches zero at 3.6298 Å,"
" 0.0005 Å below the minimum of the energy curve (3.6303 Å). \\ Near the "
"minimum, the pressure changes by about 1100 kbar per 1 Å of lattice "
"constant, so the difference of 0.44 kbar corresponds to 0.0004 Å in the "
"lattice constant."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:183
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"この差は、平面波の数が有限であることから生じます。\\ "
"エネルギー曲線は、カットオフエネルギーを一定にして計算しているので、格子を変えると平面波の数が変わります。\\ "
"一方、SCFの応力は、平面波の組を固定したまま格子をわずかに変えたときのエネルギー変化として計算されます。\\ "
"平面波が十分に多ければ両者は一致しますが、そうでなければ差が残ります。この差を **Pulay応力** （有限基底による応力の補正）と呼びます "
"[8]_ 。\\ :numref:`{number}節 <sec-cl-cutoff>` "
"で、この差がカットオフエネルギーとともにどう変わるかを調べます。"
msgstr ""
"The difference arises from the finite number of plane waves. \\ We "
"compute the energy curve at a fixed cutoff energy, so changing the "
"lattice changes the number of plane waves. \\ The SCF stress, however, "
"comes from the energy change for a small change in the lattice while "
"holding the set of plane waves fixed. \\ The two results agree when there"
" are enough plane waves, but otherwise a difference remains. This "
"difference is called **Pulay stress**, a correction to the stress due to "
"the finite basis [8]_. \\ :numref:`Section {number} <sec-cl-cutoff>` "
"examines how this difference varies with the cutoff energy."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:192
msgid "vc-relax（格子定数最適化）"
msgstr "vc-relax (Lattice Constant Optimization)"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:194
msgid ""
"QEの ``vc-relax`` は、SCF計算で求めた応力を使い、BFGS法で圧力が0になる格子を探します。\\ "
"Quloudでは、計算機能「格子定数最適化」がこの計算です。\\ 応力の収束閾値は0.01 GPa（0.1 kbar）にしました。\\ "
"開始点によって結果が変わるかを調べるため、3.56、3.64、3.72 Åの3つから始めました。\\ 格子定数の変化を :numref:`fig-"
"cl-cutoff` の右に、結果を :numref:`tab-cl-vcrelax` に示します。"
msgstr ""
"QE's ``vc-relax`` uses the stress from SCF calculations and the BFGS "
"method to find the lattice at zero pressure. \\ In Quloud, this is the "
"\"Lattice Optimization\" feature. \\ We set the stress convergence "
"threshold to 0.01 GPa (0.1 kbar). \\ To test whether the result depends "
"on the starting point, we started from three lattice constants: 3.56, "
"3.64, and 3.72 Å. \\ The right panel of :numref:`fig-cl-cutoff` shows how"
" the lattice constant changes, and :numref:`tab-cl-vcrelax` lists the "
"results."

