#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:226
msgid ""
"表の「最後のSCF」は、最適化が終わったあとに、QEが最後の格子で平面波を選び直して行うSCF計算です（出力の ``The G-vectors "
"are recalculated for the final unit cell`` ）。\\ SCFの回数には、この計算を含めていません。\\ "
"3.64 Åから始めると、3回のSCF計算で3.6299 Åに収束し、SCFの圧力が0になる格子定数（3.6298 Å）とほぼ一致しました。\\ "
"しかし、開始点を変えると、最適化後の格子定数は3.6287〜3.6302 Åと0.0015 Åの幅で散らばります。"
msgstr ""
"The \"final SCF\" in the table is the SCF calculation that QE runs after "
"the optimization ends, with the plane waves reselected for the final "
"lattice (``The G-vectors are recalculated for the final unit cell`` in "
"the output). \\ The number of SCF calculations does not include this "
"calculation. \\ Starting at 3.64 Å, the lattice constant converged to "
"3.6299 Å in 3 SCF calculations, nearly matching the lattice constant at "
"which the SCF pressure is zero (3.6298 Å). \\ However, with other "
"starting points, the optimized lattice constants spread over 0.0015 Å, "
"from 3.6287 to 3.6302 Å."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:231
msgid ""
"この散らばりも、平面波の扱いによるものです。\\ ``vc-relax`` "
"では、格子を動かしている間、開始時の格子で選んだ平面波の組をそのまま使います。\\ "
"開始点が極小から離れていると、最適化後の格子では、カットオフエネルギーで本来選ぶべき組と違う平面波で計算していることになります。\\ "
"平面波を選び直した最後のSCFの圧力（表の右端）は、3.56 Åから始めた場合で1.39 kbarと、収束閾値（0.1 "
"kbar）より大きく残っています。\\ 3.56 Åから始めた結果（3.6287 Å）を開始点にして ``vc-relax`` "
"をやり直すと、3.6299 Åに収束し、最後のSCFの圧力は0.02 kbarになりました（表の最後の行）。\\ 3.64 "
"Åから始めた結果と一致します。\\ 最後のSCFの圧力の絶対値が閾値より大きいときは、得られた格子から ``vc-relax`` "
"をやり直します。\\ やり直しでは極小に近い格子で平面波の組を選び直すので、開始点による違いが小さくなります。"
msgstr ""
"This spread also comes from how the calculation treats plane waves. \\ "
"``vc-relax`` keeps the set of plane waves selected for the starting "
"lattice while the lattice moves. \\ If the starting point is far from the"
" minimum, the optimized lattice is calculated with a set of plane waves "
"different from the one the cutoff energy would select for that lattice. "
"\\ The pressure of the final SCF with reselected plane waves (rightmost "
"column of the table) remains at 1.39 kbar for the run starting at 3.56 Å,"
" above the convergence threshold (0.1 kbar). \\ Rerunning ``vc-relax`` "
"with the result of the 3.56 Å run (3.6287 Å) as the starting point gave a"
" converged lattice constant of 3.6299 Å and a final SCF pressure of 0.02 "
"kbar (last row of the table). \\ This matches the result from starting at"
" 3.64 Å. \\ When the magnitude of the final SCF pressure exceeds the "
"threshold, rerun ``vc-relax`` from the optimized lattice. \\ The rerun "
"reselects the set of plane waves at a lattice close to the minimum, so "
"the dependence on the starting point becomes smaller."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:243
msgid "カットオフエネルギーと格子定数"
msgstr "Cutoff Energy and Lattice Constants"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:245
msgid ""
"エネルギー曲線と応力のどちらで求めた格子定数が、カットオフエネルギーに対して早く収束するかを調べます。\\ カットオフを40〜120 "
"Ryに変え、それぞれ3.60〜3.68 Åの5点でエネルギー曲線と圧力を計算し、3.64 Åから ``vc-relax`` を行いました（ "
":numref:`tab-cl-cutoff` 、 :numref:`fig-cl-cutoff` の左）。\\ "
"エネルギー曲線の格子定数は、この5点にBirch–Murnaghanの式を当てはめて求めました。"
msgstr ""
"We compare how quickly the lattice constant converges with cutoff energy "
"when obtained from the energy curve or from stress. \\ We varied the "
"cutoff from 40 to 120 Ry and, for each cutoff, calculated the energy "
"curve and pressure at 5 points from 3.60 to 3.68 Å and ran ``vc-relax`` "
"from 3.64 Å (:numref:`tab-cl-cutoff` and the left panel of :numref:`fig-"
"cl-cutoff`). \\ We obtained the lattice constant from the energy curve by"
" fitting the Birch–Murnaghan equation to these 5 points."

