#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:285
msgid "全エネルギーは3.64 Åでの値を、120 Ryの値からの差で示しています。\\ 圧力0は、SCFの圧力が0になる格子定数です。"
msgstr ""
"The total energies are evaluated at 3.64 Å and reported relative to the "
"value at 120 Ry. \\ Zero pressure denotes the lattice constant at which "
"the SCF pressure is zero."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:292
msgid ""
"左：カットオフエネルギーと、エネルギー曲線（Birch–Murnaghanの式、5点）、SCFの圧力が0になる点、3.64 Åからの ``vc-"
"relax`` で求めた格子定数。右： ``vc-relax`` （60 Ry）の各SCF計算での格子定数。0回目が開始点で、3.56 "
"Åと3.72 Åから始めた計算の最初の2点（0回目と1回目）は縦軸の範囲外です。破線はエネルギー曲線の格子定数（60 Ry、13点）です。"
msgstr ""
"Left: lattice constants versus cutoff energy from the energy curve "
"(5-point Birch–Murnaghan fit), the zero of the SCF pressure, and ``vc-"
"relax`` starting at 3.64 Å. Right: the lattice constant at each SCF "
"calculation of ``vc-relax`` (60 Ry). Step 0 is the starting point; the "
"first two points (steps 0 and 1) of the runs starting at 3.56 Å and 3.72 "
"Å lie outside the vertical axis range. The dashed line is the lattice "
"constant from the energy curve (60 Ry, 13 points)."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:294
msgid ""
"全エネルギーそのものは、60 Ryでもまだ120 Ryより5.8 meV高く、カットオフに対してゆっくり収束します。\\ "
"それでも、エネルギー曲線から求めた格子定数は40〜120 Ryで3.6301〜3.6304 Åと、0.0003 Åの範囲に収まります。\\ "
"格子定数を少し変えた計算どうしでは、カットオフによる誤差がほぼ同じだけ入り、エネルギー差では打ち消し合うためです（ "
":doc:`../kpoints/kpoint_convergence` でk点について見たのと同じことです）。"
msgstr ""
"Even at 60 Ry, the total energy itself is still 5.8 meV higher than at "
"120 Ry and converges slowly with cutoff. \\ Even so, the lattice constant"
" from the energy curve stays between 3.6301 and 3.6304 Å over 40–120 Ry, "
"a range of 0.0003 Å. \\ Calculations at slightly different lattice "
"constants have nearly the same cutoff error, so the errors cancel in "
"energy differences (the same cancellation seen for k-points in "
":doc:`../kpoints/kpoint_convergence`)."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:298
msgid ""
"一方、応力から求めた格子定数は、カットオフに敏感です。\\ 40 Ryでは、エネルギー曲線の値より0.007〜0.008 Å小さくなります。\\ "
"60 Ryでは0.0004 Åまで近づきますが、80 Ryでは再び0.0013 Å離れ、100 Ry以上でようやく0.0003 "
"Å以内にそろいます。\\ Pulay応力はカットオフを上げると小さくなりますが、この計算では単調には減りませんでした。\\ 60 "
"Ryで差が小さかったのは、偶然と考えるのが妥当です。"
msgstr ""
"The lattice constant obtained from stress, however, is sensitive to the "
"cutoff. \\ At 40 Ry, it is 0.007–0.008 Å smaller than the value from the "
"energy curve. \\ At 60 Ry, the difference drops to 0.0004 Å, but it rises"
" again to 0.0013 Å at 80 Ry. Only at 100 Ry and above do the values agree"
" to within 0.0003 Å. \\ Pulay stress decreases as the cutoff rises, but "
"the decrease was not monotonic in these calculations. \\ The small "
"difference at 60 Ry is best regarded as coincidental."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:304
msgid ""
"40 Ryを除くどのカットオフでも、 ``vc-relax`` の結果は、SCFの圧力が0になる格子定数と0.0001 "
"Å以内で一致しています。\\ ``vc-relax`` "
"は応力が0になる格子を正しく見つけていて、その応力自体にPulay応力が含まれていることが、エネルギー曲線との差の原因です。\\ "
"応力で格子定数を0.001 Åの精度で求めるには、エネルギー曲線で求める場合より高いカットオフが必要です。"
msgstr ""
"At every cutoff except 40 Ry, the ``vc-relax`` results agree with the "
"lattice constants at zero SCF pressure to within 0.0001 Å. \\ ``vc-"
"relax`` correctly finds the lattice at zero stress. The stress itself "
"includes Pulay stress, which explains the difference from the energy-"
"curve result. \\ Determining the lattice constant to an accuracy of 0.001"
" Å from stress requires a higher cutoff than determining it from the "
"energy curve."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:311
msgid "実験値との比較"
msgstr "Comparison with Experimental Values"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:313
msgid ""
"Cuの格子定数の実験値は、25 °Cで3.61491 Å（X線回折） [9]_ です。\\ PBEで求めた3.6303 Åは、これより0.0154"
" Å（0.43%）大きくなっています。\\ 体積弾性率の計算値141 GPaは、室温の実験値137 GPa [10]_ より3%大きい値です。"
msgstr ""
"The experimental lattice constant of Cu is 3.61491 Å at 25 °C, measured "
"by X-ray diffraction [9]_. \\ The PBE result, 3.6303 Å, is 0.0154 Å "
"(0.43%) larger. \\ The calculated bulk modulus, 141 GPa, is 3% higher "
"than the experimental value of 137 GPa at room temperature [10]_."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:317
msgid ""
"ただし、この差をそのままPBEの誤差と見ることはできません。\\ "
"今回の計算は、原子が静止した絶対零度の結晶のエネルギーを求めたもので、原子の零点振動も熱膨張も含んでいません。\\ "
"実験値は室温での値で、どちらの効果も格子を広げる向きにはたらきます。\\ 零点振動と熱膨張を差し引いた「静止した格子」の実験値は3.61491 "
"Åより小さいはずなので、PBEの格子定数の過大評価は0.43%より大きいことになります。\\ "
"体積弾性率も温度とともに小さくなるので、同じように比べるには温度の違いを考える必要があります。\\ "
"今回の計算の範囲では、どの効果がどれだけ差に寄与しているかは分けられません。"
msgstr ""
"However, this difference cannot be taken directly as the PBE error. \\ We"
" calculated the energy of a crystal with stationary atoms at absolute "
"zero, including neither atomic zero-point vibrations nor thermal "
"expansion. \\ The experimental values are for room temperature, and both "
"effects expand the lattice. \\ The experimental lattice constant for a "
"\"static lattice\" after subtracting the effects of zero-point vibrations"
" and thermal expansion would be smaller than 3.61491 Å, so PBE "
"overestimates the lattice constant by more than 0.43%. \\ The bulk "
"modulus also decreases as temperature rises, so a fair comparison must "
"also account for the temperature difference. \\ These calculations do not"
" allow us to tell how much each effect contributes to the difference."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:325
msgid "この数値実験から分かること"
msgstr "What the Numerical Experiment Shows"

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:327
msgid ""
"エネルギー曲線は、縮めた側で急に立ち上がる非対称な形をしていました。2次式で極小を求めると、当てはめる範囲を広げるほど格子定数が大きい側へずれ、3.60〜3.66"
" Åの4点と3.52〜3.74 Åの12点で0.004 Å違いました。"
msgstr ""
"The energy curve was asymmetric, rising steeply on the compressed side. "
"With a quadratic fit, the lattice constant at the minimum shifted upward "
"as the fitting range widened. It differed by 0.004 Å between the fit to 4"
" points from 3.60 to 3.66 Å and the fit to 12 points from 3.52 to 3.74 Å."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:328
msgid ""
"状態方程式を当てはめると、Birch–Murnaghanの式とMurnaghanの式の格子定数の差は0.0001 "
"Åでした。Birch–Murnaghanの式は、当てはめる点を13点から7点に減らしても格子定数が変わらず、13点のエネルギーを0.005 "
"meV以内で再現しました。"
msgstr ""
"Fitting an equation of state (the Birch–Murnaghan or the Murnaghan "
"equation) gave lattice constants that differed by 0.0001 Å between the "
"two equations. The Birch–Murnaghan equation gave the same lattice "
"constant when the number of fitted points was reduced from 13 to 7, and "
"it reproduced the energies of all 13 points to within 0.005 meV."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:329
msgid ""
"エネルギー曲線から求めた格子定数は、カットオフ40〜120 Ryで0.0003 "
"Åの範囲に収まりました。全エネルギーそのものが数十meV変わる条件でも、エネルギー差から求める量は早く収束します。"
msgstr ""
"The lattice constant from the energy curve stayed within a range of "
"0.0003 Å for cutoffs from 40 to 120 Ry. Quantities derived from energy "
"differences converge quickly even when the total energy itself changes by"
" tens of meV."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:330
msgid ""
"応力から求めた格子定数（ ``vc-relax`` "
"、SCFの圧力が0になる点）は、平面波の数が有限であることによるPulay応力のため、カットオフに敏感でした。0.001 Åの精度には100 "
"Ry以上が必要で、カットオフに対して単調には収束しませんでした。"
msgstr ""
"The lattice constants obtained from stress (``vc-relax`` and the zero of "
"the SCF pressure) were sensitive to the cutoff because of Pulay stress "
"from the finite number of plane waves. An accuracy of 0.001 Å required at"
" least 100 Ry, and convergence with the cutoff was not monotonic."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:331
msgid ""
"``vc-relax`` は開始時の平面波の組を使い続けるので、60 Ryでは開始点によって結果が0.0015 Å散らばりました。3.56 "
"Åから始めた計算は、平面波を選び直した最後のSCFの圧力（1.39 kbar）が閾値を超えていたので、得られた格子からやり直すと、3.64 "
"Åから始めた結果と一致しました。"
msgstr ""
"Because ``vc-relax`` keeps the initial set of plane waves, its results at"
" 60 Ry varied by 0.0015 Å across starting points. For the run starting at"
" 3.56 Å, the final SCF pressure with reselected plane waves (1.39 kbar) "
"exceeded the threshold, so we restarted from the optimized lattice, and "
"the result matched that of the run starting at 3.64 Å."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:332
msgid ""
"PBEで求めた格子定数3.6303 Åは室温の実験値より0.43%大きく、体積弾性率141 "
"GPaは実験値より3%大きい値でした。実験値は零点振動と熱膨張で広がった格子の値なので、静止した格子どうしで比べた格子定数の過大評価は0.43%より大きくなります。"
msgstr ""
"The PBE lattice constant, 3.6303 Å, was 0.43% larger than the "
"experimental value at room temperature, and the bulk modulus, 141 GPa, "
"was 3% larger than the experimental value. Because the experimental "
"values are for a lattice expanded by zero-point vibrations and thermal "
"expansion, the overestimate of the lattice constant in a comparison "
"between static lattices is larger than 0.43%."

#: ../../cu_lattice/lattice_constant.rst:334
msgid ""
"今回の結果は、Cuと :numref:`tab-cl-conditions` "
"の計算条件（PBE、PAW擬ポテンシャル、k点メッシュ、スメアリング）についてのものです。\\ "
"ほかの物質や擬ポテンシャルでは、Pulay応力の大きさや必要なカットオフが変わります。\\ 応力（ ``vc-relax`` "
"）で格子定数を求めるときは、カットオフを変えて、エネルギー曲線から求めた値とそろうかを確かめてください。"
msgstr ""
"These results apply to Cu under the calculation conditions in :numref"
":`tab-cl-conditions` (PBE, PAW pseudopotential, k-point mesh, and "
"smearing). \\ For other materials or pseudopotentials, the magnitude of "
"the Pulay stress and the required cutoff differ. \\ When you determine "
"the lattice constant from stress (``vc-relax``), vary the cutoff and "
"check that the result agrees with the value from the energy curve."

